## Findings recorded (not fixed — stop conditions)

1. Backup journal records a STALE snapshot ID for 3 consecutive runs. Cause:
   `restic snapshots --latest 1` returns one snapshot PER PATH GROUP, not one
   overall; `head -1` takes array position, not max(time). Reproduced on a
   scratch repo. Fix applied in-tree; UNPROVEN on the live host (no run since).
   -> proposals/ops-a-OPS-35.md (new item). Stays open on deployment evidence.

2. Restore drill initially reported "identical: 63, changed: 0" because it
   compared the restored tree with ITSELF ($live_root == restore target). A
   test that cannot fail. Corrected: 59 identical, 4 changed, matching an
   independent manual sha256sum comparison. -> proposals/ops-a-OPS-24.md

3. logs/ is absent from the restic path set -> a restore has no operational
   history. Not added: enlarging the approved nightly set is an operator call.
   -> proposals/ops-a-OPS-07.md

4. data/monitoring (269M) and 3 smaller data/ classes are in no path set.
   -> proposals/ops-a-OPS-09.md

5. metaread read-only role absent; provision-sales-reporting.sh reads
   /tmp/reporting-hub.sql but the file is at config/platform/postgresql/, and
   its `install A A` line is a no-op. NOT fixed: creating DB roles and reading
   wallet credentials is a stop condition. Likely a PAY/SALES item.
   -> proposals/ops-a-OPS-01.md

